🔌 reach the grove
",
}
`;

exports[`git.grove.keyrack given: [case] a vault that mangles the value when: [t0] a value is piped in then: the malfunction matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"   └─ 💥 the value that landed is NOT the value sent

💥 MalfunctionError: git.grove.keyrack: the read-back does not match
   sent:   b915470f6afcc7e5…  (16 bytes)
   landed: c33861969d1cb4ce…
   likely: the value was mangled in transit — a final newline, or a
           shell expansion on the far side.
"
`;

exports[`git.grove.keyrack given: [case] a vault that refuses the read-back when: [t0] a value is piped in then: the malfunction matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"   └─ 💥 could not read the key back

💥 MalfunctionError: git.grove.keyrack: the set reported success, and the read-back failed
   🟡 the key's state on this box is UNKNOWN — do not assume it took.
   check by hand:
     cd $HOME/git/sandpine/svc-lessons && rhx keyrack get --owner bert --key LESSON_API_KEY --env prep --value | wc -c
"
`;

exports[`git.grove.keyrack given: [case] a vault that stores nought when: [t0] a value is piped in then: the malfunction matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"   └─ 💥 the key reads back EMPTY

💥 MalfunctionError: git.grove.keyrack: the set reported success and stored nought
   the key is configured on the grove, and its value is zero bytes.
   so a clone there will fail on an absent key, with a rack that LOOKS set.
"
`;

exports[`git.grove.keyrack given: [case] an empty pipe when: [t0] the skill is invoked then: the refusal matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"✋ ConstraintError: git.grove.keyrack: the piped value is empty
   the read that fed this pipe produced no bytes — check it first:
     rhx keyrack get --owner ehmpath --key K --env prep --value | wc -c
   🟡 a LOCKED key prints its tip and pipes as ZERO bytes, so 'locked'
      and 'absent' look identical downstream. unlock it first:
     rhx keyrack unlock --owner ehmpath --env prep --key K
"
`;

